#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:15
msgid "Cppcheck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:17
msgid ""
"**Cppcheck** is a static analysis tool for C/C++ code. It provides a unique "
"code analysis to detect bugs and focuses on detecting undefined behavior and "
"dangerous coding constructs. The goal is to detect only real errors in the "
"code (i.e. have very few false positives). More information about this tool "
"on `the official webpage  <http://cppcheck.sourceforge.net>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:24
msgid ""
"Cppcheck is rarely wrong about reported errors. But there are many bugs that "
"it doesn't detect. You will find more bugs in your software by testing your "
"software carefully than by using Cppcheck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:29
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:32
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:34
msgid ""
"**Cppcheck** supports a wide variety of static checks that may not be "
"covered by the compiler itself. These checks are static analysis checks that "
"can be performed at a source code level. The program is directed towards "
"static analysis checks that are rigorous, rather than heuristic in nature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:39
msgid "Some of the defects that might be detected include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:40
msgid "Automatic variable checking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:41
msgid "Bounds checking for array overruns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:42
msgid ""
"Classes checking (e.g. unused functions, variable initialization, and memory "
"duplication)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:43
msgid "Usage of deprecated or superseded functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:44
msgid ""
"Exception safety checking, for example, usage of memory allocation and "
"destructor checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:45
msgid "Memory leaks, e.g. due to lost scope without deallocation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:46
msgid "Resource leaks, e.g. due to forgetting to close a file handle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:47
msgid "Invalid usage of Standard Template Library functions and idioms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:48
msgid "Miscellaneous stylistic and performance errors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:51
msgid "Additional checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:53
msgid ""
"Be default **Cppcheck** is configured to check the next additional defects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:55
msgid "``warning``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:56
msgid "``style``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:57
msgid "``performance``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:58
msgid "``portability``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:59
msgid "``unusedFunction``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:61
msgid ""
"The full list of supported check with detailed description is located on "
"`the official webpage  <https://sourceforge.net/p/cppcheck/wiki/ListOfChecks/"
">`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:65
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:67
msgid ""
"**Cppcheck** is implicitly used as the default check tool when :ref:"
"`projectconf_check_tool` option in :ref:`projectconf` is not set. To be "
"explicit, you can specify it in the configuration directly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:79
msgid "Useful options that can be used used for adjusting check process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:87
msgid "Extra flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:89
msgid ""
"Useful flags that can help more precisely configure **Cppcheck** to satisfy "
"your project requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:95
msgid "Flag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:96
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:98
msgid "``--enable=<id>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:99
msgid ""
"Enable additional checks. The available ids are: ``all``, ``warning``, "
"``style``, ``performance``, ``portability``, ``information``, "
"``unusedFunction``, ``missingInclude``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:101
msgid "``--std=<id>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:102
msgid ""
"Set standard. The available options are: ``c89``, ``c99``, ``c11``, ``c+"
"+03``, ``c++11``, ``c++14``, ``c++17``, ``c++20 (default)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:104
msgid "``--language=<language>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:105
msgid ""
"Forces **Cppcheck** to check all files as the given language. Valid values "
"are: ``c``, ``c++``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:107
msgid "``--inline-suppr``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:108
msgid ""
"Enable inline suppressions. Use them by placing one or more comments, like: "
"``// cppcheck-suppress warningId`` on the lines before the warning to "
"suppress (enabled by default if no extra flags specified)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:110
msgid "``--suppress=<spec>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:111
msgid ""
"Suppress warnings that match ``<spec>``. The format of ``<spec>`` is: "
"``[error id]:[filename]:[line]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:113
msgid "``--platform=<type>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:114
msgid ""
"Specifies platform-specific types and sizes. The available built-in "
"platforms are: ``unix32``, ``unix64``, ``win32A``, ``win32W``, ``win64``, "
"``avr8``, ``native``, ``unspecified (default)``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:116
msgid "``--inconclusive``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:117
msgid "Allow reporting defects even though the analysis is inconclusive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:119
msgid "``-D<ID>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:120
msgid "Define a preprocessor symbol. Example: ``-DDEBUG=1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:122
msgid "``-U<ID>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:123
msgid ""
"Undefine preprocessor symbol. Use -U to explicitly hide certain #ifdef <ID> "
"code paths from checking. Example: ``-UDEBUG``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:125
msgid "``-I <dir>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:126
msgid ""
"Give a path to search for include files. Give several -I parameters to give "
"several paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:128
msgid "``-j <jobs>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:129
msgid "Start ``<jobs>`` threads to do the checking simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:132
msgid "Suppressing warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:133
msgid ""
"It might be useful to explicitly instruct **Cppcheck** to ignore some of the "
"known defects in project codebase. Since ``--inline-suppr`` is enabled by "
"default, it's possible to directly mark pieces of code that will be excluded "
"from **Cppcheck** report using ``// cppcheck-suppress warningId`` syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:139
msgid ""
"Warning ID can be found in square brackets at the end of defect description, "
"for example: ``src\\Blink.cpp:17: [low:style] The function 'loop' is never "
"used. [unusedFunction]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:142
msgid ""
"By default, :ref:`check` command doesn't scan framework sources and that's "
"why some functions from in your project might be reported as unused. For "
"example, you can ignore warnings about ``setup`` and ``loop`` functions from "
"Arduino-based projects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:162
msgid "Addons (MISRA, CERT)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:164
msgid ""
"**Cppcheck** provides several addon scripts that analyze dump files to check "
"compatibility with secure coding standards and to locate various issues. "
"Most useful addons for verifying compliance with popular guidelines are "
"**MISRA** and **CERT**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:170
msgid "MISRA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:172
msgid ""
"``MISRA`` is a proprietary set of software development guidelines for the C/"
"C++ programming languages developed by MISRA (Motor Industry Software "
"Reliability Association).  It aims to facilitate code safety, security, "
"portability, and reliability  in the context of embedded systems, "
"specifically those systems programmed in ISO C/C++."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:179
msgid ""
"Since this standard is proprietary, **Cppcheck** does not display error text "
"by specifying only the number of violated rules (for example, [c2012-21.3]). "
"If you want to display full texts for violated rules, you will need to "
"create a text file containing MISRA rules, which you will have to pass when "
"calling the script with ``--rule-texts`` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:185
msgid ""
"In order to use ``MISRA`` addon you will need to provide a special file with "
"the description of ``MISRA`` rules. Usually, it has the next contents:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:200
msgid ""
"Next, you need to instruct **Cppcheck** that you want to run an additional "
"addon script. Since this script requires an additional file with rules, you "
"can pass it via a special ``json`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:211
msgid "Finally, add new flag to :ref:`projectconf_check_flags`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:222
msgid ""
"The full list of implemented ``MISRA`` checks can be found on `the official "
"webpage  <http://cppcheck.sourceforge.net/misra.php>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:226
msgid "CERT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:228
msgid ""
"``SEI CERT`` coding standard provides rules for secure coding in the C "
"programming language. The goal of these rules and recommendations is to "
"develop safe, reliable, and secure systems, for example by eliminating "
"undefined behaviors that can lead to undefined program behaviors and "
"exploitable vulnerabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/static-code-analysis/tools/cppcheck.rst:234
msgid ""
"In order to use the ``CERT`` addon, simply specify it as an additional flag "
"in :ref:`projectconf_check_flags` section:"
msgstr ""
